WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:15.050
Unit 2 · Logic & Reasoning · done!

3
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:21.690
Unit 3 · Shapes, Grids & Coordinates

4
00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:24.810
Chapter 1 · Shapes All Around

5
00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:32.530
Name a shape, just by counting!

6
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:37.490
Meet Aarav!

7
00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:46.970
"Find shapes in the classroom, in 1 minute!"

8
00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:56.630
Blackboard, clock, carrom board…

9
00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:06.110
How do you know a shape's name? Think!

10
00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:13.920
Count the sides and the corners!

11
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:23.360
2D shape = a flat shape you can draw

12
00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:30.800
Side = a straight edge

13
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:44.020
Corner = where 2 sides meet (a vertex)

14
00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:52.110
Triangle: 3 sides, 3 corners

15
00:01:52.110 --> 00:02:05.530
Square: 4 sides, all equal

16
00:02:05.530 --> 00:02:18.200
Rectangle: 4 sides, opposite sides equal

17
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:26.930
Square: all 4 equal · Rectangle: opposite

18
00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:39.400
Circle: no sides, no corners

19
00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:43.860
More sides → a new name!

20
00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:52.670
Pentagon: 5 sides

21
00:02:52.670 --> 00:03:02.360
Hexagon: 6 sides, like a honeycomb cell

22
00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:10.240
Octagon: 8 sides. Octopus: 8 arms!

23
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:24.840
Tip: same number of sides and corners

24
00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:28.100
Game: name that shape!

25
00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:40.340
Count the STOP sign's sides. What shape?

26
00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:49.560
8 sides → an octagon!

27
00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:58.150
True or false: a triangle has 4 corners?

28
00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:04.970
False! 3 sides → 3 corners

29
00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:11.100
Back to Aarav's shape hunt!

30
00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:17.320
Blackboard → rectangle

31
00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:23.340
Wall clock → circle

32
00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:31.060
Samosa → triangle. Yum!

33
00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:36.320
Carrom board → square

34
00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:47.890
Your turn: how many rectangles around you?

35
00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:56.950
Screens are made of tiny squares: pixels

36
00:04:56.950 --> 00:05:04.530
Game house = square + triangle roof

37
00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:14.250
4 + 3 = 7 sides altogether

38
00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:27.750
2 square windows + 1 triangle flag = ? sides

39
00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:36.500
4 + 4 + 3 = 11 sides

40
00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:44.800
Hexagon + triangle: how many corners?

41
00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:52.790
6 + 3 = 9 corners

42
00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:56.490
Your turn: practice check

43
00:05:56.490 --> 00:06:05.410
How many sides does a hexagon have?

44
00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:14.390
6 sides and 6 corners, like a honeycomb cell

45
00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:18.600
Count the sides to name the shape

46
00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:24.170
Square: 4 equal · Rectangle: opposite equal

47
00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:31.440
Triangle 3 · Pentagon 5 · Hexagon 6 · Octagon 8

48
00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.490
Circle: no sides, no corners

49
00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:40.370
Chapter 1 done!

50
00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:47.170
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
